The prime ministers of India and Japan meet in Tokyo
The new Prime Minister of India, Narendra Modi, meets his Japanese counterpart, Shinzo Abe in Tokyo to discuss ties in the field of economy and security, as part of his first serious foreign visit after winning the elections in May.
Mr. Modi is on a five-t-daiting trip to Japan in order to strengthen economic ties with the world’s third-largest economy.
At the foregoing plans to increase nuclear cooperation are at the fore.
India also reportedly hopes for an agreement on defense cooperation between the two States.
FANO will hold the final Expert session
The Federal Agency for scientific organizations (FANO of Russia), together with the Russian Academy of Sciences, will hold the third expert session "Assessing the effectiveness of the activities of scientific organizations".
The meeting will become the final in a series of meetings held by the agency within a year, according to a press release received by Lenta.Ru.
At the third meeting it is planned to sum up the work of the expert session for a year and to form a final list of indicators to assess the effectiveness of scientific organizations.
Separately, the participants plan to discuss the rules for the formation of expert groups responsible for assessing the work of scientific panels, and criteria for conducting assessments.
The third expert session will serve as the final event in a series of events for the formation of a unified approach for all three academies to the methodology for estimating the performance of scientific organizations.
Over the last five months, we have managed to do this, and the final version of the regulatory documents is negotiated.
According to the results of the immediate session, we must complete the formation of processes of scientometric and expert analysis, to agree on the stages and timing of the evaluation, ”said Elena Aksenova, head of the expert-analytical department of FANO of Russia.
The event will be attended by representatives of more than a hundred scientific institutes of Russia.
As a follow-up, the adoption of a resolution is expected.
The meeting will begin at 10 a.m. Moscow time on September 16, 2014 at the address: the city of Moscow, Solyanka street, house 14.
The scientists have found a way to detect related-full stars
Astrophysicists from the University of California in Santa Cruz studied turbulent strife and its impact on chemical homogeneities in stellar clusters.
It is expected that the discovery of specialists will make it possible to look for relatives among the stars, i.e. arising from a single cluster.
The results of their studies were published in the journal Nature, and briefly about them can be found on the website of the university.
The reason for the same chemical composition of the nearby stars is turbulent stirration in the clouds of gas, which is preceded by the formation of the stars.
Even if the born star then leaves the stellar cluster, according to its chemical composition it is possible to determine the place of her birth and the region for the formation of stars-relatives.
Earlier, the scientists had doubts that the evolution of the star outside the cluster can lead to the emergence of differences in its chemistry content from such in relatives in the cluster.
Simulation results conducted by astrophysicists show that such differences should not appear.
In their study, experts using a supercomputer simulated two interstellar gas streams, which together shaped the cloud.
This object for several million years under the influence of its own gravity is transformed into a cluster in which protostars begin to be formed.
Scientists have added mile paints to the original gas flows and found that thanks to the rapid turbulent stirring in the guinea, a high degree of chemical homogeneity is achieved.
According to astrophysicists, their study proves that it is possible to look for sorceried stars in chemical composition, as well as to determine the possible regions for the formation of such facilities.
Carrata Police Arrest 20-Year-Year-Official Charge at High Eloquence
The motorbike was confiscated after it traveled at a speed of 125 km / h in the zone with a speed limit of 70 km / h and through a bushland to hide from police in Pilbarian.
Carrat’s traffic police patrol this this morning tried to stop a blue motorbike, discovering that its velocity reached 125 km / h, when he left the service station on Batgate Road.
The police reports that the motorcyclist did not stop and continued to move around Burgess Rood, then turned into a bushland, as a result of which the cops lost sight of him.
The motorbike and the person, corresponding to the driver's description, were spotted next to Walcott's Way in Bulgarra.
Carrata police charged a 20-year-old man with a refusal to stop and dangerous driving.
It should be brought before the Carrata World Judgment on September 23.
The motorbike was confiscated and detained for three months.
The academic year in the DPR will not begin until October
On September 1, the educational year will not begin in the DPR, since only 10% of children are in the region.
This was announced by the Minister of education and science of the self-proceded republic Igor Kostenok.
According to him, 11% of schoolchildren went to other regions of Ukraine, 20% went to Russia.
Education in schools in the territory controlled by the DPR will begin no earlier than October 1.
However, the teachers will go to work on September 1.
The investigation of the TU-204 disaster in Vnukovo in 2012 has been completed
The Investigative Committee of Russia has completed the investigation of the criminal case on the fact of the TU-204 plane crash at Vnukovo airport in December 2012.
About it was reported today in the IC of the Russian Federation.
“The Moscow Interregional Investigative Investigation Department on the transport of the Investigative Committee of Russia completed the investigation of the criminal case initiated on the fact of the accident of the aircraft UT-204 of Red Wings airline at Vnukovo airport on December 29, 2012 on the grounds of a crime provided for in part 3 of article 263 of the criminal Code of the Russian Federation / violation of traffic safety rules and the operation of air transport, which negatitiated the death of two or more persons).
The reason for the disaster was the failure of the crew to perform standard procedures and an increased approach to the landing.
