Lavrov: Russia will not “slapping the door” in connection with the new sanctions and will not leave the WTO
Russia won’t sloke the door in connection with new sanctions.
This was stated today by Russian foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov, speaking to MGIMO students and teachers.
About our responsive measures in the case of a new wave of anti-Russian sanctions, then I will not even reason, to fantasize, because everything should be specifically calculated.
And when we understand what European and American-partner partners will be honored at this at this time, then we will make decisions about how to respond to it.
This will not be connected with slapping doors, some grievances, misunderstood - the minister said.
First of all, we will start from our interests, interests to protect our economy, the social sphere, our citizens, our business and will draw conclusions from the actions of the partners for their adequacy, compulsability and reliability.
According to the steps that are taken in the field of sanctions, it is very good to judicate what the partners are trying to achieve, the Russian foreign minister continued.
If it is said that "they sanctions will also be painful for us, but we are forced to do this in order to be punished by Russia," - this is probably probably not very adequate."
As for the WTO’s withdrawal of the Russian Federation in response to possible new sanctions, there is not.
On the contrary, we want to more actively master the tools of the WTO, including when it comes to trade disputes,” Lavrov Said.
We have already used this tool in order to overcome, we believe, discriminatory EU policy towards anti-dumping procedures.
According to the Minister, Russia is accused of damping and at the same time applied anti-dumping anti-dumping measures against sectors of the Russian economy.
“We are ready to use WTO mechanisms in order to defend our position on the inadmissibility to apply the norms of the third EU energy package reprospect,” Lavrov said.
