In Karelia for the sale of counterfeit money sentenced to a resident of the Leningrad region
As reported in the Republican Ministry of internal Affairs, the man was engaged in his criminal fishery in the Olonets and Segezhsky districts.
In addition to Karelia, he committed similar crimes in other regions of the country.
In particular, the accused has already managed to inherit in the Vologda region, where in the spring of this year he was sentenced to two and a half years in prison.
Later the man appeared before the Olonets district court.
And for the completion of the investigation on the crimes committed in our republic, he was transferred to Segeju.
In the course of the investigation, guilt is proved for several episodes of the sale of counterfeited money dating back to the summer of the year of 2013.
At the end of June of this year the materials of the criminal case with the indictment were sent to the court.
On Friday, August 29, the court decided to replace the period of deprivation of liberty for a four-year period with serving in a general-regime colony.
Judgments have not entered into legal force.
We will remind, last week convicted two salesmen of counterfeigned money, which were paid by them in Petrozavodsk’s stores.
Azerbaijani citizens came to Karelia from St.
One of them is deprived of their liberty for five years, the other for four.
Each is given a fine of 500 thousand rubles.
The sentenncy has also not yet entered into legal force.
In Arkhangelsk celebrated the 73 th anniversary of the arrival of the first convoy “Dervish”
The ralliance, which took place in the regional center, was dedicated to the first Arctic convoy.
"Dervish" delivered military assistance to the USSR from the United States and Great Britain.
In Arkhangelsk, a commemoration rally was held at the mortgage-of-mouth to a future monument to the participants of the northern convoy, which is located on the embernium named after Sedov in Solombala.
At the event brought together representatives of the veteran organizations of Arkhangelsk, children from the cadet-class.
For the first time we gathered twenty-three-three-three years ago, when the foundation stone was planted.
But at the same time, today's event is not a holiday, but a day of remembrance of those who were not returned to the sea, ”said Boris Karpov, chairman of the council of Veterans Veterans of the Northern Shipping Company.
Then at the event the city bnatizing orchestra acted, and pupils of the cadet classes presented flowers to the veterans and marched with the flags of Russia and Victory banner.
The ralliation ended with laying flowers to the wardrobe.
The convoy itself consisted consisted of five British vessels and one Dutch transport, loaded with strategically important raw materials (10 000 tons of rubber, 1,500 tons of uniform shoes, tin, wool and many other inventory and equipment).
In addition, on board the ships there were also military equipment and weapons - 3 800 deep bombs and magnetic mines, fifteen Harrickane fighters, dismantled in a dismantled state.
At the same time the escort of the convoy amounted to 16 ships of the British Navy, among which there were two aircraft carriers.
Caravan of ships was not detected by the enemy and successfully reached the destination - Arkhangelsk.
Of the 848 ships that took part in vital caravrantas operations, 126 transport and about 50 military vessels were killed.
In the framework of "Amur Autumn" will be a festival of an amateur cinema
From September 10 to September 12 in Blagoveshchensk there will be an Amateur film festival “KinAmur” in the framework of “Amur Autumn”.
Local film enthusiasts will be able to take part in the master classes and screenings of the festival of theater and cinema.
On September 10, the participants of KinAmura will take part in a master class of well-known directors, a creative greeting and a “Short meter” showcased: “Hello Man”, “Departing in an Orange”, “Agyny field”.
On September 11 there will be a special sequencing “Fire under the plaque” of the Amur director Semyon Rudenko.
On September 12 there will be a ceremonial closure of the KinAmura festival, which will be summed up and the winners of the festival will be announced.
An amateur-knowledge competition will be held in a number of nominees.
For the first time, cartoons will participate: 3 animated films were selected for the festival.
In total, 11 authors participate in the festival.
Next year, its participants are planned to be exposed to the Russian level, according to the press service of the city administration.
Reminiscating the very American ideal that labor rights are human rights
Congressmen Keith Ellison and Jon-Lews have proposed a bill that protects trade unions as a civil law.
“Where there are trade unions, there are middle-class jobs,” said Ellison, a Democrat from Minnesota who is co-co-support of the Progressive Faction.
That’s why I’m proud to represent the Embrlation of Employee Equities Act along with the symbol of the civil rights movement by John Lewis.
This innovative bill will give employees the same legal opportunities in discriminating against trade unions as in other forms of discriminateding, stopping the forces of anti- trade unions
Modification of the Employment Regulatory Act in such a way as to allow employees facing discrimination for participation in trade unions to seek fairness in the civil courts - and to compensate for damages and punctual allowances - a reasonable and necessary initiative.
However, of course, this is certainly not a Radical initiative - at least according to American standards.
In fact, the best way to understand what Ellison, Lewis and co-authors of the bill are proposing is to remember a very American thought.
In spite of the attacks by trade unions in recent years - in Wisconsin, Michighan and other states throughout the country - Americans once supported countries around the world to accept, enlarge and respect labor rights.
There’s been a time that millions of Americans still recognize when this country simultaneously defended democracy, freedom of speech, the freedom of the press and the right to organization.
When the United States Occupied Japan After World War II, General Douglas McArtour and his aides helped the country adopt a constitution designed to ensure that Hideki Tojo’s militarized autocracy was replaced by democracy.
Realizing that employees and their trade unions play a role in shaping a new Japan, they included a text which explicitly recognizes that “the right of workers to an organization, both negotiations and collective action is guaranteed.”
When the United States invaded Germany after World War II, Dwight General David Eisenhower and his aides helped the Germans write a constitution that ensured Adolf Hitler’s fascism had been replaced by strong democracy.
Acknowledging that Employees will need to organize and be heard in a new state, the Germans included an article that openly stated: "The right to form associations in order to protect and improve the labor and economic conditions will be guaranteed to each person and every profession or sphere of activity.
Agreements that limit or seek to imprude this right will have no legal force; measures aimed at these purposes will be found to be unlawful.
When the former First Lady Eleanor Roosevelt was chairman of the International Commission on Human Rights, which drew up the World Declaration on Human Rights, which will be adopted by the United Nations in 1948 as a worldwide agreement, Roosevelt and compilers included a guarantee that “everyone has the right to organize and join trade unions to protect their interests”.
Generations of Americans have taken for granted the basic proposition that labor rights are human rights.
When this country advised other countries on how to create civil and democracies, Americans explained that the right of organization of trade unions - and that this trade union participates as an equal partner in collective negotiations with corporations and governmental institutions - should be protected.
Now, when these rights are attacked in America, it is wise, indeed, to return to the American ideal that working people should have the right to an organization and so that their voices are heard in a free and open society.
As the Reverend of Martin Luther King Jr. Said Fifty-Yeved Years:
The story is a great teacher.
Now everyone knows that the trade union movement did not blew up the forces of the nation, but has enlarged them.
Raising the standard of living of millions, trade unions miraculously created a market for the industry and raised an entire nation to an unimaginable level of production.
Those who are attacking trade unions, forget these mercheny simple truths, but history remembers them.
The story remembers, as it owes it to us.
Appreciative recognition of labor rights as a human or human rights – and increased protection of civil rights in order to prevent discriminating against trade union organizations is long overdue.
Keith Ellison and Jon Lewis are Reviving the ideals that have historically enclosed America and made the promise of democracy a reality.
The judge is temporarily blocking a law that could clapprove all abortion clinics in Louisiana
In the U.S, a U.S., a federal judge on Sunday temporarily blockaded the Louisiana’s law that his proponents say he’s likely to close all five abortion clinics in the state.
According to this measure, which was documented by Louisiana Governor Bobby Ginadl in June and was due to come into effect on September 1, doctors who perform an abdominal would be obliged to have the authority to receive patients in the hospital within a radius of 30 miles of their practice.
Nevertheless, the decision of the judge means that at the present moment doctors can continue to have legal abortion, continuing to seek such powers.
"The plaintiffs will be allowed to work legally, continuing to take office," Judge John DE Graveles wrote.
The hearing will be scheduled within a month in which the judge will make a more permanent decision under this law.
Defendants of the right to aborts were happily greeting this decision, the latter in a series of decisions against similar measures, saying that this will give doctors more time to receive hospital powers.
“Today’s solution ensures that Louisiana women will be protected from an insidious law that seeks to deprive them of health and rights,” said Nancy Nortup, president and head of the Reproductive Rights Center, which has filed a lawsuit to shut down the law on behalf of three of the state’s five clinics.
It was not immediately obvious whether the decision applied to the doctors from the two clinics, who did not act as plaintiffs in this case, and also filed an application for admission.
Luizian is part of the 11 states that have enacted such laws, and the courts have recently recognized such measures as unconstitutional in Alabama and Mississippi.
The key parts of the Texan law, which would close most of the remaining clinics in this state, were blocked by a federal judge on Friday.
Wrestlers for abort-of-acquisition, along with the College of Obstivitants and Gynecologists and the American Medical Assisting Law, say that laws on admission powers impose restrictions on doctors, which are not necessary from the point of view of medicine.
Opponents of abortion object that such measures are aimed at protecting women's health, although some also noted their positive effect in clunaizing the closure of clinics.
It’s only one doctor who has an abdicated in Louisiana has the authority to enroll in a hospital, the Reproductive Rights Center said.
If all other doctors in the state will be forced to stop performing this procedure, this doctor, fearing for their safety, would stop performing this procedure, the group said.
Criticizing this decision, Louisiana officials said they wouldn’t penalize abductive physicians as long as their admissions await a decision.
what will lead to the imposition of quotas for domestic products
Not less than half of the products for each type of goods in the assortment of retail chains should be of Russian-produced, according to the State Duma from the faction “Just Russia” Oleg Nilov.
The parliamentarian has prepared a bill aimed at the introduction of protective measures against domestic producers, the newspaper “Izvestia” writes. “Izvestia”.
The document will still be detailed in order to avoid possible discomfort for buyers.
This applies to goods that are not produced in Russia. <...> According to the other groups of products that are produced in Russia, the retailer will have to provide at least half of their shelf to domestic producers”, – said Nilov edition.
Together with the amendments to the article "On the basics of state regulation of trading activities in the Russian Federation", the bill provides for the introduction of amendments to the Tax Code, establishing a reduced VAT rate of 10% when selling products produced in Russia.
The idea to introduce a 50 percent quota in trading networks is included in a package of stimulient measures for Russian manufacturers.
On the shelves there will be several times more domestic goods.
However, the initiative can have both a positive and a negative effect, experts say.
According to Sergey Litvinenenko, a member of Nadogovik, a member of Sergey Litvinenko, a member of an independent expert center for Public Douma Sergey Litvinenko for the Russian economy, as well as for the domestic agricultural and food industries, the effect will have a positive nature and will lead to an increase in growth.
In the plus there will be agricultural producers, farmers, small shops.
They will be able to sell more, which means that the profits will grow.
In addition, they will have the right to query retailers their conditions and prices, because they will be forced to buy their goods.
Russian manufacturers will be able to increase the volume of their activities and sales, which will lead to the payment of higher taxes than before.
This will increase budget revenues, will create new jobs, some industries will begin to expand, some quickly develop, will make a contribution to GDP growth.
Dependence of Russia on foreign food will be reduced by several times, however, not at once”, – the expert notes.
Previously, Russian enterprises often could not break into the sheaves of local stores due to the high competition from foreign analogues.
Now, after the imposition of the embargo, this niche has been vacated and you can succumb with relief.
But we should not forget that after all necessary approvals and sanitary checks, food products from Latin America, Turkey and Serbia will enter the Russian market.
In other words, now it has now come the “moment of lull”, when the previous players have already left, and the new ones have not yet come.
After almost a month we can talk about the increased demand for domestic raw materials, as well as an increase in prices for ready-made products, ”the first vice-president of the all-Russian public organization “Russian Club of Financial Directors”, Ph.D. Tamara Kazyanova told AiF.ru.
Unequitably, the idea of smolding at least 50% of Russian food products in each category will make it possible to assign the sector to local producers.
In this case, they will compete with each other, and not with the goods, which due to subsidies of another state, are cheaper.
In other words, the struggle for the buyer will unfold between companies operating according to the single laws of the industry.
On the other hand, Kasyanov notes, Russian manufacturers are able to satisfy 50% of the internal needs of comrades-in-the-creators not in all articles.
And in this situation, retail chains will have to “retach” the share of Russian goods up to half the assortment.
In this regard, there is an increasing concern that low-quality goods will arrive on the shelves.
It is possible, under the guise of those produced in Russia, foreign products with broken labels will be supplied, ”the expert adds.
The negativative effect of the introduction of quibrels will feel large retail chains, especially those who are more likely to cooperate with importers.
It is meagvidness that foreign suppliers themselves will suffer in this scenario, since the demand for their products will decrease.
Litvinenko does not preclude that the law on quotas for domestic goods can also affect consumers.
The fact is that some products of Russian-produced products may be inferior in quality to imported analogues, while the stores will be able to instill prices for the second, as for scarce goods.
Economists again talking about the forgotten idea of import substitution in the early 2000's this year due to the incessant devaluation of the ruble.
Now, against the background of difficult relations with the West, the issue of abandoning imported products is becoming even more topical.
The law is designed to oblige retailers when shaping orders suppliers to retaliate with domestic manufacturers.
Then we will go much faster and more confident on the path of import substitution, and the production planning system for the necessary types of products will be created in a shorter period of time, ”says Deputy Oleg Nilov.
Participentially effective quota mechanism will be for those agricultural sectors where the potential is especially high, for example, in the dairy industry, where the share of imports accounted for 25 per cent.
Our farmers are really able to completely cover the shelves of Russian stores.
In addition, a powerful impulse can be obtained by measles production.
As you know you know, the largest share of the import is stored according to beef - from 30% to 35%.
It turns out that 65-70% still falls on Russian products”, – says Kasyanova.
Experts are of the opinion that the introduction of quotas for domestic products will contribute to import substitution and can accelerate this process.
However, this initiative in itself does not lead to import substitution, since this requires a set of measures for this, Litvinenko is sure.
In any case, 50% of the goods sold, according to this initiative, can still be brought from abroad, which means that there will be no full-fledged import substitution, but significant steps in this direction will have been made.
In addition, it is not enough to establish quotas, it is still necessary to establish the production of domestic products in the country in order to fulfill these quotas.
These quotes just such guarantees will be provided, ”the expert says.
Unreafined Diagnosed and Lack of Access to Optimal Treatment Means ovarian Cancer in Rural Areas
Angelina Jolie and her brbe James published a video in memory of their deceased mother who died of ovarian cancer in 2007.
Propagating women in rural areas of Australia are at a higher risk of ovarian occunior deaths than those living in cities.
The researchers analysed disease maps of more than 1,100 Australian ovarian ovarian cancer in 2005, finding that only 35 percent lived five years after being diagnosed.
Lead researcher Susan Giordan of QIMR Bergheffer Institute for Medical Estucies reported that the probability of dying during the study is 20 percent higher for those who live in the regions and remote areas of the state than those who live in urban areas.
SLLURE STUDY: New Medications May Slow Lung and ovarian cancer
The researchers paspected women’s medical footsteps in seven years.
Doctor Jordan said that a woman's age at the time of diagnosis, type of ovarian cancer, the presence of current diseases and socio-economic status also affected the possibility of survival.
Older-agenåden women and those who had cancer at a later stage at the time of the diagnosis had the lowest survival rates.
For those who have lived in regions or remote areas of the state, the probability of dying during the study was 20 percent higher than for those who lived in urban areas.
Although the study wasn’t designed to determine why women living outside cities are more likely to die from ovarian germ cancer, Dr. Jordan suggested an unatcompulsory diagnosis and a lack of access to optimum treatment—possimilities.
"This disease is best treated by surgeons specializing in gynecological oncology, and they are mainly located in large cities," she said.
Despite improving the quality of telemedicine services in order to reduce the impact of the distance, she suggested that an increase in the number of out-of-hosted exit services that would allow professionals to treat women closer to the home and support programs for people being treated far from their home could help.
Doctor Giordan said that regardless of the geographical location, the study found that prolonged life expectancy among women with ovarian ovary is rare, emphasizing the need for more effective treatment and prevention.
A study financed by Rio Tinto Ride to Conquer Cancer will be Published in the Medical Journal of Australia.
In March 2011, at the age of the age of the age of the age of the age of 33, Elisha Nive, a young mother from the Golden Coast, said she had an aggressive form of ovarian cancer.
In September in the Kuzhenersky district will explodes the doors of a new FAP
The construction of a medical institution in the village of Toktiybelyak was started in April this year and was carried out according to a standard project.
the cost of work amounted to a little more than 10 million rubles.
As reported the Department of public relations and information of the head of Mari El, the financing for the construction of the object was carried out at the expense of the republican budget in accordance with the targeted investment program.
The total area of the built medical and preventive institution is almost 230 square meters.
