Turkey summons U.E. diplomat on espionage in connection with espionage
The Ministry of foreign Affairs of Turkey summoned the most high-ranking American diplomat in the country for clarification in connection with the report of American and British espionage in Turkey.
Deputy Prime Minister Bühlent said the U.S. harassed harassers and Turkish officials were discussing the announcement on Monday.
The German magazine “Der Spiegel” and the online magazine “The Intercept” reported that the documents provided by a former analyst of the U.S. National Security Agency Edward Snowden shows that Turkey was a priority object of reconnaissance for American and British intelligence services.
According to Turkish news agencies, Turkish President Recep Tayyyip Erdoğan has downplayed the importance of this message, saying that all leading countries are spying on each other.
Previously reported information that the main intelligence agency of Germany also made Ankara an object of reconnaissance, caused a more angry resonance from the Turkish government.
The Biggest Chinese Companies Unite Against Alibaba
Chinese companies, including China's largest commercial real estate developer Dalian Wanda Group and Internet Giants Tencent Holdings (occ networks, messenger, etc.) and Baidu (largest a Chinese search engine), are creating a company that will compete in an online trading market with Alibaba.
However capturing the miracle of the Chinese Internet, which left behind even its American rivals - eBay and Amazon.com, it will not be easy.
Union of the Largest
The companies plan to invest 5 billion yubans ($ 814 million) in a joint venture, 70% of Wanda will own Wanda and for 15% - to each of the Internet companies, Wanda Group said in a statement.
It is planned to re-register a company in Hong Kong.
The joint venture will combine Baidu search services with the popular social platform WeChat (the largest social network in China whose number of users is about 438 million people), Tencent and Wanda infrastructure.
In addition to a network of 40 luxury hotels, Wanda Group manages at least 49 commercial real estate sites throughout China and 40 shopping machinations.
Last year the company invested 50 billion yuan (more than $ 8 billion) in the construction of a film studio and an amusement theme park in Qindao (the city in eastern China on the coast of the Yellow Sea).
It is expected that the project will attract more than 1 million visitors every year and make a profit of $ 960 million.
In addition, Wanda owns an American chain of cinemas AMC Entertainment Holdings, which makes the company the largest operator of theaters in the world.
By 2015, Wanda plans to equip its shopping machinations, hotels and places of entertainment with e-commerce services, the development of which will be carried out by the newly created rival of Alibaba.
According to Doong Tse, which will lead the new company, thanks to Wanda will be able to increase the number of users of its e-commerce services from the current 40 million people to 100 million by next year.
The new site should become the world's largest online-to-offline platform, says Dong Tse.
The elusse of online-to-offline (O2O commerce lies in attracting buyers on the Internet so that they come to ordinary offline stores or to buy other traditional services.
A classic example of O2O are coupon services like Groupon or Vigoda.ru
“O2O is the largest cerepox in online commerce,” Wanda CEO Wang Jianilin (quoted according to Bloomberg).
“There’s no real O2O site in China right now, and everyone’s odds are approximated in this situation,” he said.
The Chinese e-commerce market is the largest in the world, and McKinsey & Co. is estimated to have increased more than three times by 2015 compared with 2011, to $395-bill.
The number of Chinese Internet users has risen to 632 million, Bloomberg cites official statistic reports: this is more than the population of any country in the world, with the exception of India.
And according to forecasts, by 2015 this number can grow up to 850 million people.
Union of the Worth
The head of Tencent Ma Huaten until recently was the wealthiest man in China, however, according to the index of millionaires of the Bloomberg agency, the founder of Alibaba Jack Ma has already overtaken him by $ 5.5 billion.
The fortune of Jack May is estimated at $ 21.8 billion, of which $ 11 billion falls on his stake in Alibaba.
Baidu CEO Robin Lee now occupies the third place among the wealthiest people in China, while Wang Jianlin from Wanda is the fourth line of the rating.
“It’s very interesting to watch this battle: the three wealthiest people are joining forces to challenge an even richer man,” the Chinese e- Commerce Research Center in Hangzhou Cao Lei told Bloomberg.
But he believes that the new company is not likely to be able to seriously compete with Alibaba immediately after creation: “Roman can not be built in one day”.
The fact that Alibaba is not so easy to rank not only to new companies, but also to the well-deserved leaders of the world e-trafficking, is evidenced published on the day before by a report on Alibaba for the last quarter.
Alibaba is often described as an interverge between eBay and Amazon.com, but from April to June the Chinese company earned more than both of its American competitors combined.
The net profit of Alibaba for the period is almost two times higher than a similar combined indicator of competitors - it has grown almost three times a year and amounted to $ 1.99 billion.
“Alibaba still has a huge potential to generate money, largely due to its mobile applications,” an Analyst from the Hong Kong Arete Research Service said.
According to an updated prospectus of Alibaba on the website of the US Securities and Exchange Commission, the number of active mobile users of the company's services in July amounted to 188 million, which is significantly higher than the March figure (163 million people).
At the same time, 32.8% of all Alibaba transactions over the last quarter accounted for mobile devices.
Alibaba will have to name the value of its shares before an IPO.
According to an average assessment of 11 analysts interviewed by Bloomberg, the company can be estimated at $ 187 billion after the sale of the shares.
according to Bloomberg sources, the debut of Alibaba on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) can take place on September 16.
Road-show the company, preceding this event, will start on September 3.
It is expected that Alibaba’s IPO will become a record-breaking in NYSE history and will allow the company to attract about $ 20 billion.
Until now the record in terms of the volume of funds raised on the US stock exchanges belonged to the Visa payment system, which in 2008 conducted the initial placement of its shares, earning $ 17.9 billion on this.
Not less than half of food products in retail chains should be of Russian-produced, according to State Duma deputies.
They've drafted a bill on the subject.
We are talking about introducing amendments to article 8 of the Federal law “On the basics of state regulation of trade activity in the Russian Federation” and the Tax Code.
The purpose of the document - the introduction of protective measures with regard to Russian food producers.
An important refinement, according to the bill, at least 50 percent of the products of domestic production in the stores should be for each type of product.
However, the document will take into account that there are goods that are not produced in Russia, for example, vegetables and fruits in the winter, so there will be a “discount” for them in order to avoid possible discomfort for buyers.
Simultaneously, the draft law introduces a change in the Tax Code of the Russian Federation, which establishes a reduced VAT rate in the amount of 10% when selling all food products, whose country of origin is Rosity, Izvestia reports.
On August 27, a draft law was submitted to the lower house of parliament on amendments to the Federal Law "On Retail Markets", which proposes to revive farm markets in Russia, in which small manufacturers will be able to sell their products.
Magaluf’s police chief charged with irritation
The plaintiffs presented evidence of extortion by police and officials of the municipality of Calvia in the office of public prosecutor Mallorca on Friday.
Calvia police chief on the resort island of Mallorca was arrested as a result of accusations of corrosion from businessmen and owners of bars in the indisclosed antiquities of Magalufe.
Chief inspector Jose Antonio Navarro was placed in detention resulting from allegations of trucinations inflicted against him by several businessmen from Punta Bullen, the street where most of Magalouf’s bars and nightclubs.
Mallorca Diario, the plaintiffs presented evidence of extortion by police and officials of the municipality of Calvia to Mallorca anti-errectal prosecutor on Friday.
Another two local police officers were arrested by the guards of the National Guard of Spain in connection with allegations of corrupt and will be questioned by the judge together with Navarro.
The Spanish daily ABC reported that dissatisfactory owners of nightclubs say that protectionism from the authorities is seriously reflected in the state of their business.
“It’s nothing more about earning money, we’re talking about survival,” one of the businessmen told the court.
It is impossible to jeopardize our sources of existence.
We don't have anything to lose.
Magalouf came into the headline of the international press this in the summer after a popular video on YouTube, which showed an 18-year-old British vacationer who made blowjobs to 24 men during a bar race.
The authorities of the island since then have been trying to stop hooliganism in a rationential state among Magalouf vacationers, reducing to a minimum the number of insocrated alcohol races on bars.
In addition, the Playhouse club, where there was an incident with a blizzard, was forced to close for a year, while Playhouse and organizers of Carnage bars together were fined € 55000 ($ 73000).
Magalouf’s tourist resort, mainly popular among young British holidaymakers, has also been a site of numerous alcohol-intoxicated accidents associated with insensible amusement, known as “balconing” when people jump from one balcony to the other or from a balcony to a hotel swimming pool.
The first day of spring is marked with wet and wind conditions that affected flights at Adelaide Airport
SPRing prepared a cold surprise in the south of South Australia, bringing torrential showers and strong winds, which affected flights at Adelaide Airport.
Another 5 mm of the rain fell on the city in the evening for 9 p.m, after 6.6 mm, which oscorted for the night of Sunday.
The last rain was preceded by a pair of short showers with gusty wind, including a thunderstorm, which began shortly before 8 in the evening and spilled almost 4 mm in about 10 minutes.
After the winter issued an early portion of spring last week, the temperature again fell on Monday to a maximum of just 15,8C in the city.
Squamighty conditions, as expected, served as one of the reasons for the delay in the landing of Virgin Airlines flight from Melbourne to Adelaide.
The aircraft was supposed to land on schedule immediately after 7:30 pm, but fell into the wind shift zone - a sudden change of speed or direction of the wind at a short distance - and was forced to gain a height.
wind gusts reached 50 km / h on the ground at Adelaide Airport at this time.
The flight data showed that the aircraft had to gain a height during the second landing, and the plane eventually landed at about 8:40 a.m.
Debate of this flight caused a subsequent latency of several other voyages, including an Emirates flight from Dubai and the Qantas flight from Sidney.
A maximum of 16C is predicted in Adelaide on Tuesday with a probability of one or two downpours.
Calculation of the estimate of construction objects in the Russian Federation will take place in a new
Issues of pricing, regulation of the construction industry, as well as the problem of connecting to the networks the Federal Antimonopoly Service takes special control.
The FAS has created an expert council for the development of competition in the construction sector.
At its meeting, the head of the department for the management of housing and communal services, construction and natural resources of the FAS Vadim Solovyov said that "today the calculation of the estimate of construction sites is absolutely incomprehensible."
Normative base makes pricing opaque and can lead to an unreasonable construction price, according to the FAS.
And they propose the cost of construction of state-owned facilities at the design stage to determine on the basis of market prices of structural solutions, instead of today's estimated norms and single prices for technological operations.
These proposals are included in the “road map” and are now under consideration in the Ministry of Construction.
“The replacement of the traditional estimated documentation in the construction for the calculation of the structural elements should lead to less corruption in the industry,” Vadim Solovyov explained to RGB.
After all, now every boulevoke and nut are calculated in the estimates, and it is not always possible to check everything, so sometimes unscrupulous construction companies can burial “whole tractors”.
In Minstroy we agree with the FAS.
“There are already the first developments on the transition to the calculation of the cost on the structural elements: methods have been developed to calculating the prices of constructive solutions, compiling ppaging estimates for these indicators,” Elena Zhukova, head of the department of urban planning and architecture of the Minskstroy, told RGB.
The field of road construction was chosen as a Pilot.
However, experts believe that the problem is much more serious.
Anatoly Demyanko, the head of the company "Profi-Invest", told "RGB", the estimated standards have long become obsolete, but business has not yet been pronounced another mechanism.
“As for the proposed calculations on constructive elements, in practice this is difficult to implement, since completely different technologies are often used in the construction of buildings,” he said.
It is not a secret that the construction market develops largely due to the state order.
According to Ekaterina Lezina, Chairman of the Management Board NP "Ex-expenditentiary Community of Soldiers of Public Order", today the state is the most solvent-missile customer.
Vladimir Malakhov, deputy director for the engineering of the Rosatom's sectoral center of Rosatom, drew attention to the fact that today the market is conditionally divided into companies that have access to the portfolio of contracts, and companies that own monopoly competencies and do not allow competitors on this field.
He believes that the creation of a transparent market is possible only provided that access to the contracts is maximally fenced from someone's influence manager.
At the expert council it was proposed to form a public order system in such a way in such a way that the performer does not have the right to receive more than one contract in the amount of more than 1 billion rubles.
In Minstroy it is believed that this approach needs to be evaluated from the point of view of influencing business, as well as the effectiveness of construction management.
Elena Zhukova explained, in this case it will be Necessary to give the customer the functions of the general contractor, which will lead to an increase in the number number of the customer and the budget expenses for its maintenance.
At the same time, the specialists of the customer will have to have the knowledge that allows you to assess the quality of the works performed by the contracting organizations, as well as their safety.
It will often be necessary to determine who will be responsible for the security of an object as a whole.
In addition, this approach can lead to an outflow of highly qualified participants in public procurement due to disinterprising in obtaining a state order for an indifferent volume of work and a small amount of the contract.
The Deputy head of the expert-consulting center of the Procurement Institute Alexander Evstashenkov believes that now the procedure of the state order has turned into a business game for attentivity of the contractor.
And he gave such an example: "the participant when filling in the application must indicate "concrete indicators" without specifying the words: "or the equivalent", "must be", "from", "more", "less", "an analogue", "type", "similar type", "not below", "lower", "above", "couled", "malisome", "may be", "previously", "previously", "not earlier", "not above".
Purchasengers often abuse their right to establish requirements for the content of an application submitted by contracting.
According to Yevstashenkov's 44-FZ, another problem, became the need to assess at the stage of applying the quality of work through the "waste" proposal of the participant.
Considering the application of the participant, it is actually possible to assess only the qualifications of the contractor, but not the quality of the work, the performance of which has not even even begun, the expert believes.
the quality of work can be evaluated only when accepting them.
An expert council was also invited to move the marginal income from the upper echelon, so that the intermediate contractors would disappear.
The Chairman of the expert council, the state-secret secretary, the Deputy head of the FAS Andrey Tsarikovsky believes that this should not be done, since the general contractor should be responsible for the order.
And otherwise it will turn out, as in the well-known reprise of Arkady Raikina "Athelia": "Is there a claim against buttons?".
Israeli Kids Receive to School After Gaza's War
Thousands of Israeli children in areas close to the Gaza Strip went back to school on Monday after they spent the summer in bomb shelters as rockets and deforest fell on their settlements during a 50-day war between Israel and Hamá’s, while schools in the Gaza Strip remained clairvoyed while the territory was recovering.
Beginning of school classes brought a sense of joy and unleissument to the settlements of southern Israel affected by missiles, but traces of the fighting remained fresh.
In the southern city of Ashdod, employees of the Pashosh kindergarten, in which the rocket hit, removed traces of fragments from the walls and skaters before the arrival of disciples.
"We are a little afraid, but we are happy to look to the future," said Ronith Bart, a resident of Kibbutz Saad and an English teacher at his school.
Many of the children in our area really need to return to a measured life.
Her 11-year-old, Shani Bart, said that suddenly to start going to the school “a little strange.”
“There was a difficult time and we didn’t get out of their homes at all,” she said.
President Reuven Rivlin visited kibbutsa, which is located close to the Gaza border to express his support.
Before the cease-claving agreement stopped the war last this week, thousands of residents of border settlements, such as Sa'ad did not go out or left their homes, driving away to safer areas farther from the Gaza Strip to escape rocket and mortar fire.
Many residents of Nahal Oz, settlements close to the Gaza border, where a fragment of a Palestinian mine killed a four-year-old boy was killed, they doubt that they should go back.
The Ministry of education reported that about a dozen families have not yet come back.
Their children were sent to other schools for this time.
Prime Minister Benyamin Netanyahu visited a school in Sdereto, a city on the border with Gaza, which suffered a lot from Palestinian fire.
He advised the children to study diligently and said: “We will do everything we can to provide you with knowledge and to ensure your safety.”
Israel and Hamas agreed to an truce last Tuesday.
The cease-cease agreement immediately put an end to hostilities, but key issues remained unresolvable, for example, the demand of the removal of the Egyptian-Israeli blockade of Gaza and for the opening of airports and sea ports in the Gaza Strip.
“Azerbaijan wants Hamas to lay down their arms and return the bodies of two Israeli soldiers who died in the war.
It is expected that a new stage of indirect negotiations will begin later this month in Egypt.
More than 2,100 Palestinians were killed in the war, including three-quarters by peaceful citizens and at least 494, according to an estimated Palestinian side and the United Nations.
“Israel is contesting these figures and alleges that at least half of those who were killed by militants; despite this, it did not provide substantial evidence confirming the claim.
On the Israeli side killed 66 soldiers and six civilians, including one Thai worker.
During the fighting Hamas and other militants of Gaza fired 4591 units of missiles and mines on Israeli cities, mainly in the south of the country.
In the meantime, the Israeli army carried out more than 5000 air and other attacks.
As a Rescue of Israeli attacks, thousands of houses in the Gaza Strip were damaged and demolished, an estimated 250000 people have taken refuge in more than 100 schools that have been transformed into shelters.
Because tens of thousands of people were still in the orphanages, and the fighting went on, the officials responsible for education last week postponed the beginning of the academic year.
“I hope that the school will soon be opened so that we will be able to complete our educators, like children around the world and Jewish children,” said Mohammad Amara, a 13-Year-Old boy who now lives in Gaza’s schools.
According to the popular criterion, real estate prices showed the greatest winter growth for seven years.
RP Data CoreLogic Hedonic housing value index rose 1.1 per cent for housing prices in the U.S. capital rose 1.1 per cent, RP data said on Monday.
This increase led to a cumulative increase for June, Jury and August by 4.2 per cent, the largest increase for the winter months since 2007.
An annual increase in prices amounted to 10.9 percent, more than twice the growth for 12 months by August of 2013, but the increase was not evenly distributed throughout the country.
The director of the RP data research, Tim Lawouses, announced that Sidney and Melbürn are leading a two-tiered market.
