The Ministry of economic development wants to accelerate the growth of the market of electric vehicles
This week the Ministry of economic development will submit to the government a comprehensive plan for the development of environmentally friendly transport in Russia, said the Deputy Director of the Department of the Ministry Oleg Pluzhnikov at a round table, which held "Vedomosti" at the Moskovsky Motor Show - 2014.
The plan was drawn up on the instructions of the government, one of the main goals is to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.
It is expected that the document will be adopted at the end of September - beginning of October, says Pluzhnikov, the proposed measures apply to electric cars and hybrids - there is already a plan for the development of vehicles on gas engine fuel in Russia.
The “Vedomosti has a copy”) is designed for 2014-2017
It will be necessary to develop criteria for the assessment of electrical and hybrid transport and to decide how to stimulate the use and production of environmentally friendly vehicles.
The report of the government, which will describe tax and customs measures to support electric transport, will be prepared by December 2014; the scheme of preferential lending and preferential leasing will appear by April 2015; and proposals to reduce the price of machines, stimulate the localization and the creation of service infrastructure will be developed by October 2015.
In 2014-2015 it is planned to make changes to regulatory legal acts in order to facilitate the conditions for the construction of a charging infrastructure (in parking lots, gas stations, etc.).
In addition, federal officials are going to formulate proposals for the regional authorities during 2015 so that they will also stimulate the use of environmentally friendly transport - in the form of providing it with an advantage when driving and parking, for example; and by February of 2016 - and proposals to expand public procurement of such transport.
Finally, by October 2014, the Ministry of Economic Exploration will include criteria for assessing the activities of regional authorities, reflecting the effectiveness of support for the production of environmentally friendly transport, the development of charging infrastructure.
The market of electric cars in Russia is only being shaping - about 100 electric vehicles have been sold throughout the country in 2013.
At the beginning of 2014, the import duty on electric vehicles was zeroed, so sales will amount to about 500 units, Andrei Pankov predicts the chief executive of Mitsubishi Motors in Russia.
But the five-fold growth does not make electric cars any noticeable: in 2013 in Russia, according to the Association of European business, 2.78 million passenger and light commercial vehicles were sold.
For so far, only Mitsubishi Motors imports electric cars into Russia.
Renault is being prepared to start the import - the company focuses primarily on corporate clients, says Nikolay Remise, director for strategic planning and partnerships of Renault in Russia.
The majority of other manufacturers of electric transport took a wait-and-continued stance against Russia.
The development of electric vehicles also has Russian manufacturers - "", GAZ, "", but the production is miserable.
For example, in January-July 2014, according to “ASM-holding”, “AVTOVAZ” produced 30 electric vehicles.
Demand is low due to the high cost of electric cars, the Director of AvtoVAZ for engineering Sergey Amanov admits, there will be no state support for a breakthrough in this segment.
The development of the Russian market of electric vehicles, in addition to the high cost of cars (those electric cars that are sold in Russia, on average twice as expensive than analogues with internal combustion engines) restrain the underdevestiment of the charging infrastructure (gases - units), sighs the General Director of "Autostat" Sergey Tselikov sighs.
Due to the high price and low rates of decline in the cost of electric cars in the next 3-4 years will remain a niche segment of the Russian market, the editor-in-and-of-the-in-premises predicts the editor-in-chief of Avtorevu Mikhail Podorozhansky, Tselikov agrees with him.
Car manufacturers, on the contrary, they say that some models of electric cars are already close to the cost of ordinary.
The Russian market of electric cars has good prospects, the main thing is to instill confidence in consumers that “electromobility” is real; this, in particular, the emergence of new charging stations will contribute to the emergence of all new charging stations, said Wolfgang Schlimme, president of the BMW group in Russia.
Such infrastructural projects are implemented, for example, the state-owned company "Rosseti": several stations have been built in Moscow, about $ 80 more will appear soon.
Negotiations about the construction of a network of gas stations are conducted with other regions.
According to the director of the Rosseti department of Vladimir Sophina, the company believes in the market of electric vehicles and is ready to build gas stations throughout the country, but there are also problems: a small number of electric cars in the country and the absence of a single standard for charging electric vehicles of different brands.
In addition, "Rosseti" as a grid company does not have the right to engage in the sale of electricity, it is worked out the ability to do this in relation to charging electric vehicles.
Pankov considers the most effective measure of state support for the formation of an electric vehicle market in Russia to zero customs duties.
The zero rate will be in effect until the end of 2014, the possibility of its re-extended, expanding its preferential list is being worked out.
The replacement of the transport tax on environmental (the idea is being discussed and applies to all cars) will also support the market, but it is not as noticeable as customs preferential, Pankov believes.
The transport tax in Russia is small, says Pankov, in contrast, for example, from Norway, where the reduction in tax has led to a sharp increase in sales of electric vehicles - now they account for 12% of the market.
In Russia we also need stimulant measures for car owners, for example, free parking in the city center (as they have already done in Moscow), Punkov is sure, or the possibility of moving electric cars on allocated lanes, which in Russia is not yet available.
