Will Rosneft Reimburse $140 Million of Losses
The head of “Rosneft” Igor Sechin said that the company is assessing the damage from the shelling of the Lysychansky refinery in Ukraine at $ 140 million.
About it, he said in an interview with Spiegel.
“We are estimating the damage of $ 140 million and we will negotiate with the Ukrainian government on the payment of compensation”, – said Sechin.
According to him, the commissioning of Lysychansky refinery modernized by the company was planned in 2014.
However, part of the plant was destroyed by Ukrainian artillery.
There weren’t fights there, there weren’t entrenched insurgents, but Ukrainian artillery destroyed part of the industrial facility.
In addition, the technological oil pumped into the pipes has disappeared,” he said.
We will remind, on July 18, in connection with the shelling of the Lysychansk Refinery, an oil storage reservoir burned down and the buildings of two warehouses were destroyed.
Lysychansky Refinery - the main oil reprocessing plant in Ukraine, the first prite of the enterprise was put into operation in October 1976.
The total capacity of the Lysychansk refinery is about 7 million tons of petroleum raw materials per year.
The plant is able to release the fuel standard "Euro-4", as well as batches of dysland of the "Euro-5 standard".
In March of 2012, oil supplies to the Lysychansky Refinery were suspended in connection with its unprofitability.
It was decided to start repairs at the enterprise.
A year later, Rosneft received the Lysychansky Refinery along with other Ukrainian assets of TNK-VR.
