Twitter has tried to become more interesting for new users
The microblogging service Twitter has alternated the process of registering users in order to quickly involve new participants in an active interaction with the platform.
This measure should reduce the number of microblogged people who have abandoned their microblogging.
Now the new users of Twitter will view a large number of accounts recommended during registration in order to immediately compile your circle of reading.
The recommendations are compiled on the basis of the interests indicated during registration.
At the same time, Twitter automatically specifies a Tank on a subscribing for all automatically selected accounts.
Because of this, the user will have to recapture ticks personally, so as not to read those who are not interested in him.
If earlier users of the microblogging service saw only avatar of recommended users, now Twitter displays a sample of one of the blogger’s popular tweets to help make an immemorial about a person.
This is the largest change in the Twitter registration page for the last three years.
Recently, Twitter is actively working to modernize the service.
Such an activity relates, first of all, to the continuing attempts of the service to achieve break-even.
In 2014, the microblogging service was faced with a slowdown in the growth of the user’s base and a drop in the activity of readers.
The company at the moment desperately desperately needs a large number of consumers loyal to a resource, who, having come across, would remain for a long time.
Only in the same way it is Possible to ensure a stable flow of advertising means.
