The exchange rate of the dollar has risen against MICEX above 37 rubles on the news about new sanctions being prepared by the West against Russia.
It’s a new historical record.
Dollar calculations "tomorrow" to 10:29 MSK grew by 26.9 kopecks and amounted to 37.02 ruble, the euro rose by 30 kopecks - to 48.73 ruble, according to the Moscow Stock Exchange.
Bivalve shopping cart grew by 28 kopecks compared to the level of the previous closure and cost 42.28 ruble.
Prior to the Crimean events, the dollar reached a maximum of February 19, 2009 - then it cost 36.43 ruble, and on March 3, 2014, it was already 37,005 ruble.
On the night of August 2, the White House reported that U.S. President Barack Obama and German Chancellor Angela Merkel are discussing the possibility of imposing additional sanctions against Russia.
Weakening the ruble has a long-lasting in nature, coupled with the euro, and in tandem with the dollar.
The long-neutral forecast presupposed this mark, says Anna Bodrov, a senior analyst at Alpari.
Everything that is connected with Ukraine, in one way or another, will be reflected in the courses.
As long as this continues, investors will respond.
Rumors about the invasion of troops have not been confirmed on either side, but the market turned out to be very emplative.
All the talk that he was resistant to such news, yesterday were crossed out.
The week, according to the forecasts of the specialist, will close to about these levels - 36.90 and 37.05 ruble per dollar.
The tax period has ended, oil prices are weak, politicians, sanctions, the problem of gas transit through Ukraine are all links in the same chain.
It is also predicted the acceleration of inflation: from 5 to 10% will be vaccinated for current prices in the autumn.
Soon, in addition, seasonal vacillations and fruits will run out, and there will be a certain vacuum while the networks refocus on other suppliers.
“The doll came to the mark of 37 rubles, passed it and came back, there is some powerful tantrum, – says Konstantin Bushuev, the head of the analysis of the markets “Otkrita Broker” Konstantin Bushuev.
We’re still going to see if there will be sanctions on Saturday, how NATO will meet.
The ruble, according to him, sharply weakened after the end of the tax season, then there was news on Ukraine, moreover, the Central Bank last week said that until the end of the year it completely shifts to the floating exchange rate and refuses any currency interventions.
If you look at the daily oscillation, it did not differ from the previous ones during this month, everyone was fascinated by the mark of 37 rubles, the Analyst continues.
And so, in terms of the turnover, nothing powerful has ever happened.
Anxious times for the foreign exchange market, let’s responsive at the end of January there was an increased demand for the foreign currency, as well as the third of March, when the Central Bank lowered a record amount of the currency.
UFS IC also sees the positive side of the ruble’s depreciation.
First of all, this is an increase in the revenue part of the budget from export operations, as well as an increase in the competitiveness of domestic producers due to an increase in the cost of imports, says the chief analyst of UFS IC Alexei Kozlov.
Negative moments include the rise in price of imported goods and services.
Sharp oscillations of the Russian currency significantly reduce the attractiveness of investing in the Russian economy, provoke an increase in inflationary pressures and, as a result, cause an increase increase in borrowing of funds, which, in turn, hinders the development of the country's economy.
If we talk about the stock market, the depreciation of the ruble somewhat smoothes the decline in stock prices, expressed in rubles.
For example, MICEX index during trading on Thursday decreased by 1.67%, and the RTS index lost 3.27%.
Such a significant difference in the relative decrease in indices is explained by the weakening of the ruble during the day by more than 1.5%.
Weakening the ruble is emplary in nature and is explained by the massive desire to buy currency.
As the practice shows, gradually the emotions fall to nothing, and ruble quotes partially or completely restore lost positions.
“I believe that soon we will be able to see the ratio of the dollar and the Russian currency near the level of 36 rubles per dollar”, – said Alexey Kozlov.
Genetical Distillery Is Often Misdiagnosed
The British woman said that she spent many years, thinking that she was going to die after an improplied diagnosis.
Karin Rogers spent most of her thilioctling a thilitics, thinking that she had only a few years to live, after she was diagnosed with another disease.
In fact, she had Sharko-Marie-Tut disease, a group of hereditary disturbance, which lead to damage to the nerves outside the brain and the spine.
Charitable organization CMT UK reported that an improperized diagnosis is a common problem among people with SMT, because so little is known about this condition.
Approximately 23000 people in the U.K., presumably, there is presumably SMTC that can cause motor symptoms such as muscle weakness, an insecrucited gait and crumpled toe to your toes.
Patients can feel numbness or pain, and the condition does not heal and progresses, which means that the symptoms increase over time.
When Rogers was 13, she thought she was suffering from Friedreich atensic (AF), a convoy for which was very bad.
Rogers thought she'd be confined to a wheelchair when she'd be 18 and she'd die before she'd be 30.
The mother of the two children, which is now 51, said: “I knew I couldn’t do what the others.
I fell every day, and it took me a lot of time.
“I’ve never been able to crawl on videos or skateboard with other children, and I’ve done a lot of fun at school because I’ve walked and ran.
Rogers said that when she was 13, after a length of operations to unleash an Achilla tendon and straighten her feet, she looked into the medical record when her doctor got out of the room and it was written that she had an AFF.
“I felt guilty, because I stuck my nose where I didn’t, and so I didn’t tell anyone, but I came back home, found information about this condition in the library and wrote to the AF Association,” she said.
When I received the information in response, I was shocked and experienced the most terrible pancake that was possible.
I'd think I'd be in a wheelchair at 18 and I'm going to die before I'm 25, and that I'd gradually lose all of my abilities at that time.
I went through this alone, and I planned my own funeral.
She said that by the time when she turned 17, she realized that her ability to walk didn’t get worse as she thought and asked her doctor.
He just stood up, hugged me and said: "My darling, I don't think you have this disease, because you'd already be in a wheelchair."
I'm guessing you've got something that poses a much less threat to life.
After a number of genetic examinations, she was diagnosed with SchMT.
“When he explained what SchMT is, I Thought I was pulling a lucky ticket,” she said.
Charitable organization of the UK CMT announced a month of information about SchMT in order to try to draw attention to this disease.
The tax brute force of employees of the Washington zone grows as the economy recovers
Reimbursing economics means more customers, more sales and new jobs.
This also means higher taxes.
Accounts for the payment of taxes on the state and at the local level for companies throughout the country increased moderately last year, when the economic recovery accelerated, according to a new study published last week and companies in the St.Doesse zone is not an exception.
Companies in the county, Maryland and the Virgenia cumulatively repaid $27.6 billion to the state treasury and at the local level in fiscal year 2013, 3.8 percent more than $26.6 billion collected for 2012.
The tax brute force for business and at the local level last year increased by 4.3 per cent to $671 billion, compared with 3.9 per cent a year earlier, and this was the third consecutive year-largest year of stature over the years when accounts declined in 2009, in 2009 and 2010.
Taxes levied by the state have risen faster, 4.3 per cent than local taxes, 3.9 per cent, according to a study conducted by a company providing professional services, Ernst & Young and the State Taxation Center, a tax policy group.
More than half of tax revenues in the county, 56 per cent, accounted for taxes on entrepreneurs, while 36 per cent of Maryland’s tax revenue comes from firms.
Virngia, with 28 percent, brings the smallest amount of tax revenues, proportionally, from entrepreneurship.
To a large extent, the growth of tax revenues is caused by a return to the previous level of the value of the real estate of the companies, the researchers said, raising real estate taxes by 3.7 percent this year after three years in a row, when an increase of less than 1 per cent.
While a large share of these revenues falls on large states, such as California, New York and Texas, it seems that the same thing is taking place in the Sthante zone.
Companies in the county, Maryland and Virginia cumulatively paid $10 Billion of Real Equity Taxes by the State and at the local level last year, $9.6 billion more than 4.2 per cent growth in 2012, compared with the previous year.
However, an observable return on real estate does not have any similar effect on an increase in tax revenues in the state and at the local level in Maryland, where real estate taxes barely exceed one-fifth of the company's tax accounts.
The companies of Virgina and the district of Columbia pay about half of the state tax and at the local level in the form of real real estate taxes.
“What’s going on in Marylín is that so much of their real estate, especially the tax base around the District of Columbia, belongs either to a government or a non-commercial organization that doesn’t pay real property taxes,” said Douglas Lindahlom, executive director of the state’s Taxation Center.
Thus, Maryland is forced to rely much more on, for example, on income taxes to pay the same services that are available in other states.
The recent increase in tax revenues from entrepreneurs can not be completely explained by the restoration of the real estate market.
Revenues of entrepreneurs also seem to be recovering, according to these data.
Soccer companies in the region queried a $2.3-billion corporate income tax, $2.1 billion more than in 2012.
Maryland has collected $1 billion in corporate income tax revenues, most of all in the region.
Although trends are directed in the same direction in the same direction, the tax burial of entrepreneurs at the local level does not increase at the same rate in all three areas.
The growth level in the district of Columbia was at the same level as the national average, 4.3 per cent, while growth in Maryland was significantly faster, 4.9 per cent.
Only in Virgina there was an increase in tax revenues below an average of 4.1 per cent.
Wirzine had the lowest corporate income tax of the three jurisdictions (each of which has the same corporate bet), equal to 6%.
In Maryland the corporate bet is 8.25 per cent, while in the district it is relatively high - 9.975 per cent.
A similar study of the US Chamber of Commensurum earlier this year found that Virginia has lower taxes for state entrepreneurs and at the local level and, in general, a more auspicious climate in terms of taxes for entrepreneurship than in Maryland.
The county hasn't been evaluated in this study.
Despite its adversity, Virgenia is experiencing competitive pressure from its neighbour from the south.
Northern Caroline recently signed a legislative dedication that reduces the corporate bet this year from 6.9 per cent to 6 per cent, just like in Virginia, the rate will drop to 5 percent next year.
If the state continues to achieve tax remittance targets next year, this law could bring an incremental tax rate for Employees even 3 per cent by 2017.
In the meantime, a small business in the St.’s St.’
Taxes for Entrepreneurs, payable in the form of an individual income tax by small-document, a transitional structure according to which the majority of small-old firms are arranged - in the Columbia, Maryland and Virgina district rose 20 per cent last year to $2.4 billion, at a much higher rate of growth than taxes for entrepreneurs as a whole.
The researchers are saying that the trend and increase in business tax revenues throughout the country will most likely persist this year, with the receipt of turnover tax in the state and at the local level, which grew by 6.2 per cent for the first three quarters of 2014, compared with the same period last year.
However, the St. Washington zone may lag behind, as a decrease in federal spending affects the labor market in the region.
Bronze Circum avenue of Russian Judo
The home world judo championship brought the national team of Russia two silver and seven Bronze awards.
According to this indicator, the Russians lost only to the main favorite of the competition - the national team of Japan.
The tournament in Chelyabinsk began on Monday, and the first day brought the Russian team a silver medal.
Its owner was Beslan Mudranov, who acted in the category of up to 60 kilograms.
At the same time, in an equally final struggle with Boldbaatar Ganbat from Mongolia, only one renegotiation, received by a Russian, resolved the outcome of the confrontation.
But the second day of the tournament became the most successful for the national team of Russia - on Tuesday, three medals were won at once.
In the men's competition in the category up to 66 kilogram silver went to Mikhail Pulyaev, and Bronze - Kamal Khan-Magomedov.
In the final fight, the Russian lost to the world champion in 2011 and 2013, Japanese Masasi Ebinama.
Khan-Magomedov, in the quarter-final stage who lost a compatriot, victoriously walked the consolidating tournament and became the owner of a Bronze award.
Natalya Kuzyutina also reached the third footstep of the pedestal of Honour.
In the semi-finals, she lost to the current world champion Mailinda Celmendi from Kosovo, which at this championship performed under the flag of the International Judo Federation and successfully defended the title.
In an argument for bronze, Kuzyutina was won against Ma Yinan from China, but after graduating from the tournament admitted that the third place is not exactly what she was counting on.
And again the baptism on the path of the Russian to gold was Celmendi, who defeated Kuzyutina earlier in the final of the European championship.
On the third day of the tournament in Chelyabinsk bronze was put by Musa Mogushkov, who competed in the category up to 73 kilogram.
In the quarter-finals his offender became the former representative of Moldavian Viktor Skovortsov, who now competes for the UAE team.
However, then the Russian won two fights and became the owner of the award.
Mogushkov competed in the home championship with an ankle injury, which he plans to heal in the near future, and will take a pause in the competition.
As for the ex-Moldova Skvortsov, then he and he at this tournament reached the bronze medal.
It is an interesting fact that his other compatriot, who took the sports citizenship of the UAE, Ivan Remarenko with a bronze completed a performance in the category of up to 100 kilograms.
The fourth day of the 2014 world Cup also brought the Russians one bronze, which in the category of up to 81 kg was conquered by Ivan Nifont.
In the difficult battle of the small final, he, due to the remark from the opponent won the Frenchman Alan Schmitt.
On Friday at the tournament played three sets of awards at once, but the Russians, according to tradition, limited themselves to one bronze in the men's tournament up to $ 90 kg.
Cyril Issues became its holder, and the Russian national team this medal was guaranteed: his opponent in the consolidating final was compatriot Kirill Denisov.
However, the battle itself did not take place: the opponent of the Question could not come to tatami due to an injury.
Masculine bronze was conquered by the hosts on the sixth day of the competition - Renat Saidov was put in the treasury of the pregnitentiary, who competed in a category of more than 100 kilogram.
In the consolidating final, he defeated a clear victory over the Brazilian, David Moura.
Thus ended an individual part of the world championship.
On the last day of the tournament in Chelyabinsk, on Sunday, the titles of world champions were played in team competitions.
Both the Russian teams - both male and female - were one of the main contenders for awards, but, as well as in individual competitions, representatives of the beautiful sex were unlucky - they didn't get to the medal.
But the Russian judokas won team silver.
In the decisive confrontation, in a steadfast fight with a score of 2-3 lost to the main favorites of the competition - the team of Japan.
At the same time, the Russian national team conducted 2-0 after the pure victory of Khan-Magomedov and voivoy - Denis Yartsev (weather of up to 73 kg).
However, in heavier weighting categories, Murat Khabachyrov (81), Magomed Magomedov (90) and Aslan Kambiyev (100) could not cope with their Japanese rivals.
According to the same scenario, the Bronze match in the women's tournament was also developed, where the Russian national team, leading 2-0, lost to the russians - 2-3.
At the team competition in Chelyabinsk was attended by the President of Russia Vladimir Putin, who after graduation congratulated the men's team on the silver.
“The second esterable place is very honorable, but I want to say that it was clear that you could become champions,” Putin said, quoted by RIA Novosti.
To lose to the Japanese, the founders of judo - there is nothing shameful here.
But I'm pretty sure you can't win from them.
The national team of Russia performed much much better than a year a year ago at competitions of this level, which took place in Rio de Janeiro.
Then in the asset of the Russian team there were only three medals - one silver and two bronzes.
At the same time, Olympic champions Arsen Galstyan and Mansur Isaev missed the current tournament.
Of course, we’re all big maximalists.
Yes, I want gold medals.
But let's remember that if a person in the Olympic cycle is included in the top eight, then he is the potential winner of the Olympics.
Moreover in such a kind of sport as judo”, – summed the results of the tournament the Minister of Sports of the Russian Federation Vitaly Mutko, whose words are quoted by the press service of the championship.
The national team of Japan expectedly became the best in Chelyabinsk, gaining 11 medals of various merits, five of which turned out to be gold.
The next world championship will take place next summer in Astana.
