On sale the debut album of Royal Blood - a new hope of British rock, which brought the rock duos from the clubs directly to the stadiums.
The Royal Blood duo is only a year on the stage, but already owns a nominee for a BBC music award, a trolling tour with Arctic Monkeys and a visit to the wizard of the New York concert from Jimmy Page himself.
Their unlearned eponymous Album a few months before the release received 100 thousand pre-orders, and the contract for its release lies in the Portfolio of the Warner Music.
Taking into account the current deplorable situation in the musical market, the situation out of the ordinary, because we are not talking about a new Lana Del Rey or another sweet-voice representative of the “new R'n'B", but about a duet of obscure-shaped Britons playing with the level of volume and intensity, which was the last vocabulary in fashion a couple of decades ago.
In general, bets on the first album in connection with all the above-mentioned circumstances were especially high and have already been fully justified.
The duo not in vain took a name for itself, on which they could encroach only very desperately voyage metallhydrates, and the bleed of which kings flows, as it seems to them in their veins, is also understandable.
We are talking, of of course, first of all about the heroes of the last level Led Zeppelin: as well as the great quartet, Royal Blood aims to shaking the stagnant blood of British rock, bringing it to a new height.
To make predictions about the success of this enterprise so far is, perhaps, early, but something can already be said.
A dozen songs that met in thirty for a short minute - it is not so much a demonstration of a phenomenal composer's gift, but a confident and powerful declaration of inconceiving.
Some measures of individual numbers, of course, can not be denied: for example, the pilot single "Out Of The Black" is characterized by the fact that it is not memorized with a melodical line, but a drum part.
The musicians jokingly say that this song is generally easier to be knocked out than sing.
It is also worth highlighting a powerful "Little Monster" and closing the album "Better Strangers" with a Shakespearean quote in the title.
However, it’s the truth is that each of these songs will sound great at a heavi-rocking party, but when playing in a row they merge in a more or less homogeneous canvas.
And this is not necessarily bad, even on the contrary.
The strength of Royal Blood is that they don't claim the laurels of Lennon and McCartney (shoucratically swept at Motörhead's successors), but brought numerous rock duos from ghetto indie clubs.
Their music, despite some variety, is created for stadiums, in a room designed for less than a couple of thousand people, it obviously cramped.
The secret is partly the cunning use of the bass, which replaced the guitar in the usual format, coined at the beginning of zero The White Stripes.
However, it's not only about the tools, but also the very approach to songwriting.
Heroes retrororoek zero were very difficult to choose beyond the post-modernist paradigm, with great reluctaneously went to recognize themselves not only as epigones, but independent creative units.
Royal Blood already sounds so powerful and blasphemous that this pressure successfully drapes some of the secondary and chorobthiness of the musical material.
In the end of annie, who said that the rock should be smart?
Amazon To Buy Twitch for $1.04 Billion
AMAZON has just unveiled what Information reported on Friday Morn's morning: the online store - and a video producer and hundreds of other things - is buying Twitch streaming for $1.04 billion ($US970 million).
This news came as a surprise not because no one was expecting Twitch to be sold, but because a lot of people were expecting YouTube to be a buyer.
Three months awrily selling Twitch video service Google for a good billion looked completely ready, and such a combination looked natural.
Twitch, founded only three years ago as Justin.tv, has set the goal of being a streaming service of a general nature - a real-time YouTube version.
