Photo: Alexander Myridon, Kommersant
Sanctions Mentale Menu
On August 6, President Vladimir Putin signed a decree on the application of certain economic measures to ensure the security of Russia, which are mainly called food sanctions.
It is forbidden to import beef, pork, meat and poultry, meat delicacies, meat delicacies, fish, mollusbs, milk, yoghurts, cottage cheese, vegetables, fruits, nuts, sausages and sugar syrups into the country.
The restaurants began a leapfrog with the suppliers: prices for products have increased, it is necessary to urgently look for analogues from other countries.
This will have the strongest effect on expensive restaurants with the monocooker of France, Italy and Spain, to which products were supplied directly from “matrinal” countries.
The caterpillar had to be reorganized before.
For example, when in early 2014, the Rosselkhoznadzor banned the import of Australian beef, and a year earlier - American and Canadian meat.
In return, the suppliers established beef deliveries from Argentina, Uruguay and New Zealand.
But the sanctions of the summer-2014 turned out to be much more serious.
However, on August 20, Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev approved amendments to the presidential decree, which deduce from the ban of Atlantic salmon fry and trout, lactose-free milk, seminal potatoes, sugar corn, peas and sowing onions.
Italian Valerio hopes that the sanctions can still soften.
In the meantime, part of the restaurants exist in conditions of uncertainty.
According to Vostok-West, one of the largest suppliers of HoReCa, the share of imported products in the premium segment amounted to up to 70%.
Expensive restaurants will have to change the menu for what local farmers and other countries produce,” says Serhiy Mironov, restaurategoer, the owner of Restconsultation.
If the chef is a strong chef, it won’t be a problem.
Only we have very few such chefs, and the development of a new menu can take two to three months.
The trigel from the restaurant "Braserie Bridge" is ready for this: you will have to abandon 10-15% of the dishes, another half of the menu should be recycled.
In restaurants with a mixed kitchen, dishes have already begun to be replaced, such as marble beef bee steak, says Sergey Mironov.
Cheeses from Europe can be replaced with Russian, Belarusian cheeses, cheeses from Serbia, Argentina, Tunisia, Chile, - the representative of the company "Vostok-West" Oksana Glybchuk lists the representative of Vostok-West.
Churnuts and dairy products from Europe have analogues in Russia and Belarus.
Chicken from the United States can be replaced by a Chicken from Russia and Belarus, salmon and salmon from Norway - salmon, salmon, trout from Belarus and Chile.
The absence of vegetables and fruits of European production can be compensated due to the products of domestic producers, offers from Serbia, Moldova and China.
According to Mironov, it will be easier to reorganize budget chain restaurants than the premium segment: it is unlikely that gourmets went there, able to dissIFIC Italian mozzarella from the Russian.
Although it will be difficult for Ginza Project establishments, he said.
Ginza Project has a few dozen restaurants under different brands and its own menu.
A lot of time will go to replace,” Mironov said.
Ginza renounced comments, claring the absence of owners in the country.
Owners of Caucasian Caucasian and Central Asian Cusmebrary Cusmebrium Emphasizes that products from the former Soviet republic are more fragranter than European
