Kolbai hasn’t been removed yet to a single meal.
Timur Lansky, the owner of Chaikhon N1 restaurants with Uzbek cuisine, the sanctions also do not bother: he will have to change only the laziness for New Zealand.
If Russia adjusts imports from Uzbekistan, Azerbaijan and Kazakhstan, we will even win in price, for us it will be arrogant than imports from Europe,” he says.
From the CIS you can cheaper to get clipping, larns, tomatoes, cucumbers, fruits.
At the same time, what is brought from Central Asia, much better than "plastic" from Italy, Spain and Turkey.
About Uzbek tomatoes everyone knows that they are tasty, sweet.
No one speaks like this about the Spanish.
After the imposition of sanctions, the representative of the Ministry of agriculture of Uzbekistan Olymboy Artykov said that he plans to increase the export of tilt vegetated products to Russia by halving by 2016.
About their intention to replace European imports in Russia almost immediately after the imposition of sanctions was announced by Belarus and Kazakhstan.
