“A moose for restaurants you can calmly be replaced with other salmon fish from the Far East,” says Philip Galkin, the owner of a fish bench “Your people”.
We are catching a Greek, keta keta, kernel, hustle and gauge salmon.
Yes, they are not as greasy as Norwegian salmon, because it is a wild fish.
Norwegian salmon is an aquaculture.
You're picking him up - he doesn't even move.
And you can't keep our Far Eastern salmon in your hands.
Only institutions without special claims agree to replace the Italian mozzarella
In the window of his tent are shrimp with the tag "Magadan", cod, oglu, muksun, muzzles from the Crimea, scallops from the Far East.
Galkin is confident that it is high time to switch to fish from the Far East.
According to estimates, fishing in Russia in 2013 - more than 4 million tons, a significant part of the fish goes to Japan, Korea and even in the United States.
Import of fish in 2013 - about 800 thousand tons.
The store "My own people" has been operating since 2012, sells fish through an online store, before the imposition of sanctions served another one and a half dozen restaurants, such as "Simultaneous things".
Galkin received applications from another 15 restaurants.
The same trunks can be made from our fish - it's turbulent.
We're unleabbing, we've tried different recipes.
Now we are selling sushi through an online store for a million rubles a month.
Our fish is several times cheaper, and the delivery is a maximum of 15 rubles per kilogram.
Convicized in Galkin shatra, I am preparing a portion of “Philadelphia” with a keta.
In contrast to rolls with salmon, these have to chew longer, but the consciousness that this fish is our, domestic, gives its strength.
On the website of the store "Your people" there are even rolls from halibut and sea perpetuates.
In Sushi-bars, however, replace Norwegian salmon is preferred to Chilean.
Galkin explains this by the fact that chefs come up with new recipes with the Far Eastern fish.
“The suppliers have not yet offered Russian fish to us”, – gives his explanation the owner of Killfish Bar Dmitry Yevseyev.
Approroximately the same situation with other products: Russian manufacturers could occupy a vacant niche, but this does not happen.
Boris Akimov, founder and co-civitator of LavkaLavka project, now we can talk more quickly about the substitution of imports from Europe and America with imports from China, Israel and Latin America.
There are large transnational corporations, which have powerful logistics and large volumes.
They are able to quickly replace banned imports, in contrast to our farmers.
That is, large producers of other countries will benefit from the ban," Akimov said.
Nevertheless, in the last month, the restaurant industry received a more alarming signal than grocery sanctions.
According to the basis of mass unscheduled inspections of Rospotrebnadzor was temporarily suspended the activities of three McDonald's enterprises in Moscow and two regional enterprises in Stavropol and Yekaterinburg.
“We are studying the essence of the claims presented to determine the actions necessary to open restaurants for visitors as soon as possible”, – said “Dengamum” the press service of McDonald’s.
In fact, no one really understands what will happen next.
If everything is limited to grocery sanctions, this is one option that you can survive,” says an employee a company engaged in restaurant consulting on condition on an anonymity.
If they start to close McDonald's throughout the country, then the scenario will be very different.
"EuroProtocol" instead of a traffic police incompetent
Casco payments can be obtained without a traffic police certificate - so the Central Bank intends to stimulate the introduction of "Europprotocol" in Russia.
the Bank of Russia has developed a draft of instructions, according to which from September 1 of this year to receive payments on casco an insured motorist will be able to do without a traffic record.
However, we are talking only about those cases when the accident has been formalized according to the "Europrotocol" without the involvement of the traffic police.
That is, if the accident involved only two cars, there are no physically injured persons, the damage does not exceed the established limit and both drivers reached an agreement on the question of who is the culprit of the accident.
From August 2, the limit of payments for "Europrotocol" is 50 thousand rubles, and from October 1 in Moscow, St. Petersburg, as well as in the Moscow and Leningrad regions, it will be increased to 400 thousand rubles.
The essence is that often even with minor turmoil, in a situation where an Accident can be ocdemnated according to the “Europrotococle”, drivers who have fallen into an accident cause traffic police.
After all, in the presence of casco, it was not possible to obtain a refund for it without a traffic police certificate.
Parameters spelled out in the draft instructions are just designed to eliminate this obstacle to the introduction of “Europrotocol” in Russia.
According to them, the maximum payment for casco in connection with an Accident deculivating without traffic police officers should not be lower than the limit on the “Europrotocol”.
But at the same time, it can not be higher than the limit specified in the casco insurance contract.
The idea, of course, is useful and theoretically able to unload both traffic police officers and roads.
But, most likely, neither motorists or insurers will not be enthusiastic about it.
The latter are already talking about a serious threat of an increase in scam, which can lead to the imposition of new rules of payments on casco.
As for the drivers, it is difficult to imagine what kind of work you will have to do in order to overcome ancestral Russian conservatism.
The driver in most of the cases will wait for the inspector for hours to issue a minor accident, because it is more reliant.
And yet it is not yet known that it will be easier - to defeat the scammers or to convince the drivers in the reliability of the "Europrotocle".
Sabotigating certificate will be made nominal and irrevocable
The Ministry of Finance wants to ban savings certificates for the bearer, but it will allow the banks to make them an equivalent of an irresponsible contribution.
The Ministry of Finance is preparing a bill, which will forbade savings certificates for a bearer.
Recently, this tool is gaining popularity, since the rates here are higher than on bank deposits.
The fact is the fact is that beneficiary certificates do not fall into the deposit insurance system, and they are cheaper for the bank, since it is not necessary to make contributions to the Deposit Inassurance Agency (DIA).
The spiciness of the situation is that this step is planned to be taken because of small and medium-sized banks distributing such certificates, and Sberbank and the Bank of Moscow will suffer from it, which, according to the DIA, control 98% of the profile market.
And the share of the Bank of Moscow, according to calculations of the Agency, is about 3.5%.
The problem, explained in the DIA, lies in the fact that customers of a small bank who bought such a certificate, in the event of a revocation of his license trying to receive money in the DIA.
Some depositors, without possessing sufficient financial literability and buying savings bearer certificates, can assume that their investments are insured.
The justified absence of insurance payments for these certificates in the event of revocation of a license from the bank can lead to malformation and social tension.
In the practice of the agency, there were cases in which the holders of bearer certificates tried to recover insurance indemnity through the court," the DIA said.
The problem, of course, contigurious.
After all, no one will still be able to pay certificate buyers anyway, since by law they do not have the right to recompense from the state.
If the fact is that the instrument is not insufficient in the DIA, together with it, metal bills would also be prohibited, on which the funds of citizens are accounted for in grams of one of the four metals - gold, platinum, platinum and pallad.
After all, these invoices also do not fall into the deposit insurance system, but no one is encroached on their existence yet.
It is most likely that bearer certificates are a very convenient security, which in fact can act as quasi-denes.
At the same time, their movement is practically uncontrollable: any client of the bank can buy a certificate, transfer to any citizen, and before cashing, such a certificate can be resonated by many owners.
It is no coincidence that the bill stipulates that the savings certificate must necessarily be a personal security, which must be stored in an depository.
And in order to sweeten the pilutter of banks, such certificates are allowed to be issued without the right of early repayment.
That is, an analogue of an irrevocable contribution is introduced, which bankers have been dreamed of for a long time.
