Germany will send 30 anti-tank complexes to Iraq
Germany will supply weapons to Iraq to confront militants from the terrorist group “Islamic state”, ITAR-TASS reports on August 31, referring to the decision taken at the end of the meeting of representatives of the German government headed by Chancellor Angela Merkel.
It is reported that Germany will send 30 man-portable anti-tank missile systems “Milan” and 500 wardrobe missiles to them, as well as 8 thousand G3 and G36 assault rifles.
Deliveries will be carried out by the end of September.
In addition, it was decided to allocate another 50 million euros for humanitarian assistance to Iraq.
On September 1, Madam Merkel will make a government statement on this topic in the Bundestag.
Until now, Germany did not supply its weapons to “hot spots”.
Opinions of the residents of Germany regarding the sending of weapons to the Irakists were divided.
Some believe that this is the only way to stop fighters from the “Islamic state”, others are afraid that these weapons may eventually fall into the hands of terrorists.
Militiamen shot down a Ukrainian patrol boat in the Sea of Azov
Donetsk Militaries shot down a Ukrainian patrol boat in the Sea of Azov, ITAR-TASS reported on August 3.
According to the available data, this happened in the Taganrog Bay near the settlements of Shirokino and Bezimenny (10-20 km to the east of Mariupol).
A number of Ukrainian media reported on the shelling of two boats of the coast guard.
Clarifies that the incident took place today at about 16:20 GMT.
Teenagers were picked up by helicopter from the Blue Mountain
TWO gencoder Bushookers were taken by helicopter to a safe location after spending the night, stuck in the Blue Mountains of New South Wales.
A 16-year-old girl and an 18-year-old boy went on a hike shortly after noon on Sunday in Goetts Lip in Blackheite.
Terrified relatives called the police around 8 p.m. when they didn't come home.
A search team was dispatched, which included local cops and a rescue detachment, and the couple was found around 11 p.m. near Brydal Veil’s waterfall.
The girl injured the knee, and the young man fell and bruised his head.
The officers stayed with a couple for the night, and they were picked on a swan on Monday in the morning.
They were taken away by ambulance in a stable state of Blu Mountains.
Met with two unions
Negotiations at the highest level in Minsk did not solve the problems for which they were convened, but generated a new format: the first officials of the European Union met with the first persons of the future of the Eurasian
Albehesitant on an alarming question (the situation around Ukraine does not endure”, the leaders of the EU and the Customs Union for the first time discussed a number of “hot problems”.
whether such a structure is able to work effectively, it is incomprehensible; but it is clear who withdrew the cream from this summit.
Issues in this regard blurted off on the evening of August 26, when the Belarusians, followed by other Eurasianists with the Europeans, saw new President Lukashenka in the telenoun.
The Belorussian leader set an exemployment of honed struggling, it was the behavior of a person who had just disrupted the jackpot - and is planning a worthy old age in a high-profile society.
How Maidan Lukashenko Helped
The arrival of three main European commissioners (EU ministers), who met with Lukashenko and allowed him to speak at a final briefing on their behalf - not just legitimizing the president with 20 years of experience.
This is an application for the recognition of Minsk as a full-fledged subject of European policy and the main mediator of the Ukrainian crisis.
Denis Melyantsov, a Senior Analyst Analyst for the Belarusian Institute for Strategic Studies, I am sure: from now on, Bruss will no longer be able to talk with Minsk in the same tone as before.
“The fact that Katrin Ashton has encountered tete-a-tete with Lukashenka gives reason to believe that relations with the European Union will ripen further,” he said.
This iceberg has a hidden part: preparations for the breakthrough of the Belarusian authorities began long before the November Maidan in Kiev - in the summer of 2013.
“Developments were also been achieved with the EU - these are successful negotiations to simplify the visa and the readmission, and negotiations on international security were held with the United States.
The United States even lifted a few sanctions.
As for the Ukrainian events, they themselves and the reaction of the Belarusian leaders to them only spurred this process.
Minsk, on the one hand, managed to maintain relations with Ukraine - warm enough so as not to lose too much in mutual trade, and President Poroshenko could come to Belarus for talks.
On the other - the Belarusian leader, who did not recognize the annexation of the Crimea to Russia and called to punish pro-pro-Russian militias in the Donbass with energage, did not quarrel with Moscow.
Minsk did not withdraw either from the Customs Union or the CSTO, and a Russian air base is stationed in Baranovichi.
Brussel and Washington noticed a balanced position of Minsk on the Ukrainian issue - and evaluated it, Belarusian experts believe.
How successful Lukashenka’s movement to political dilution will be will be, it will be visible from how often in the near future, Minsk will have to accept meetings in the format of the EU+TS.
In the press service of the High Representative of the EU on foreign policy and diplomacy Catherine Ashton could not promptly respond to questions about what Brusssel expects from relations in a new format.
Spokesman Ashton Maya Kocijancic only told Ogonka that, against the background of solving the issues of war and the world, this topic is not a priority.
At the same time, there were reports that the next meeting place on the Ukrainian issue with the participation of first-lying persons in a new format can be Kazakhstan.
The tar drip for Minsk was the statement of President Nursultan Näzarbayev, in which he admitted that he, it turns out, was personally asked by representatives of the European Union.
Nevertheless, at the final briefing, Alexander Lukashenko made it clear that all parties do not mind Minsk to remain a central platform for the meetings both in the format of Russia-OSCE-Ukraine and at the level of the heads of state and high representatives of the European Commission.
This means that the “the last dictator of the Europe” acquires the status of quite handshake European leader, which helps to solve a global problem.
The best friend of the European farmer
Already the composition of the delegation of the EU, which included European commissioners on trade and energy, pushed to the conclusion: the main background of the summit is not the tragic situation in the Donbas, but the economy.
In fact, the schedule of future negotiations on the supply of gas and to overcome the concerns of the CU countries on Ukraine’s association agreement with the EU seems to be an achievement more large-scale than peaceful declarations without specific dates and figures.
Commertra commissioner Karl De Gucht, however, noted that the representatives of the European Union “came in Minsk to look for a solution to a political crisis, which has economic consequences, and not the other way around.”
It seems, however, that the economic crisis in Ukraine is “working” for Belarus.
Its aftermath - and, first of all, the mutual sanctions of the West and Russia - give Minsk, which so far itself is experiencing sanctions pressure, a long-awaited field to maneuver.
Yaroslav Romanchuk, the head of the Research Center Misez, the former presidential candidate of Belarus Yaroslav Romanchuk, European investors are actively interested in the possibilities of Belarus for the supply of agricultural products to the Russian Federation bypassing sanctions.
At the same time, supply schemes are put forward, for which Vladimir Putin squeeved Minsk at the summit.
“Initiators of these diagrams,” Romanchchuk “Ogonyok”, – are not Belarusian businesswomen, but Russian companies.
For a long time they worked out schemes of deliveries of goods, including from Poland, Germany, Lithuania, and today these schemes have been destroyed.
Russian business is in dire need to somehow restore them, even through the intermediation of Belarusian structures.
The second-tonuity, the expert continues, is connected with the fact that many Ukrainian companies do not acquie a way to organize production in Belarus from Ukrainian raw materials also with an orientation to the Russian market.
Ukrainian producers have about $ 4 billion of exports to Russia, and Belarusian production and trade schemes can now be very in demand.
According to Romanchuk, the role of the owner of the platform for negotiations of the EU and TS is ideal for Lukashenka and from the point of view of developing economic ties with Europe.
He recalls that the losses of the agrarian sectors of the EU from Moscow sanctions are estimated at 5-10 billion euros, and the European Commission has currently offered agrarians only 125 million euros of compensation.
The Belarusian president can invite Brussels to work together to minimise the implications for Eurofarmers.
This can raise Lukashenko’s credibility in the EU for an unpreceinable height.
Hospitability without initiative
Katrin Ashton thanked the Belarusian authorities for the initiative to hold the summit.
But the paradox lies in the fact is that the official Minsk from its active role in the birth of the TS + EU format is denied, and the Belarusian leader at a meeting with his Ukrainian counterpart stressed that the initiator of the new format was Kiev.
“This was your proposal to get together, to discuss without any piston, not from the bay-junge to make a decision, after the signing of the Association Agreement with the EU, to understand the situation that at that time was developed in Ukraine”, – he appealed in front of the cameras to Peter Poroshenko.
However, observers interpreted this as an attempt to reassurate Moscow, according to corrects, initially it was initially against the intermediation of Minsk, which greatly increases its political weight.
In the Belarusian diplomatic department dirly emphasizes that Belofas in the organization of interaction between the EU and the CU on its own land does not pursue mercenary goals, but the ultimate goal of this format is to create a common economic space from Lissabon to Vladivostok.
“This is absolutely in the spirit of those concepts that in other spheres, in particular in the field of security, puts forward and promotes the leadership of our strategic all-Union – the Russian Federation”, – told “Ogonyok” in the foreign Ministry of Belarus, the Agency, which recently scrupulously select words.
In Moscow may there will be zones with a paid entry
The government of Moscow is considering the option of introducing zones with paid entry as a method of combating congestion of central roads by analogy with other major cities of the world, reports M24.ru with reference to the deputy mayor of Moscow for transport Maxim Liksutov.
One of the options, which has successfully established itself, is a paid entrance.
This is an expert opinion, we will definitely study it, let's look at all the disadvantages and pluses.
To talk about the fact that some decisions have been made on this, it is still too early,” Liksutov said.
Deputy Mayor stressed that for the authorities of the capital very important the experience of Asian cities, which in terms of structure and congestion are similar to Moscow.
One of the solutions taken from these countries is the already implemented construction of the central ring road, Liksutov added.
Having recently begun the construction of the Central Ring Road is an example that it does not necessarily pass all the traffic through Moscow.
If there was a sufficient detour infrastructure, then it was not necessary to have transit traffic in Moscow”, – said the Deputy Mayor.
Maxim Liksutov also said that the introduction of paid parking significantly unraveled the capital's streets.
And, according to him, the capital authorities do not plan to dwell on what has been achieved.
We will remind, on August 26, the mayor of the Russian capital Sergey Sobyanin took part in the ceremony of laying the construction of the first launch complex of the Moscow Central Ring Road (TKKAD).
