Politic reform is the main source of tension in Hong Kong, since Chinese party leaders are afraid that the call for democracy will spread to other cities.
Following Beijing's publication of a document describing China's control of Hong Kong in June, activists of the democratic movement held an unofficial referendum on elections in the special administrative region, and hundreds of thousands went to the business center of the city and staged a segregated strike.
Briefing Li is organized by the Hong Kong Government and the Chinese Lisci-Hubs Office in Hong Kong.
