Developed a potential way to steal photos of nursed celebrities
A massive break in star accounts may have been triggered through a Vulner in the Find My Phone app.
Potential scenario of the events described the resource The Next Web.
Github was published the script in Python, which allowed you to select passwords for Apple’s Find My Phone service.
This service allows you to monitor the location of the iPhone.
To access it is used the same bundle bundle of the Apple ID login and password as to access the Apple iCloud, from which photos of celebrities were stolen.
Script allows you to find the password from Find My Phone.
With this method, all sorts of combinations of symbols are consistently introduced, beginning with the most frequently used passwords.
The author of the script claimed that the service of Find My Phone the number of entered variants of passwords is unremittered.
If you correctly organize the security system after several unsuccessful attempts to enter an incorrect password, the account must be blocked and inform the user about an attempted burglary.
Due to the Vulner, the users did not receive any messages about an attempt to choose a password to their account.
Hackers recognized the password from the Apple ID and used it to access iCloud.
According to Hackapp user’s message on Twitter, the vulnerability was discovered two days ago, on Saturday, and written a script program for the selection of passwords.
At the moment the Vulnerability is closed: after five attempts, access to the service is blocked.
The resource contacted the user Hackapp and he noted that the above-mentioned vulture is characteristic of many services, but noted that there is no evidence that such a vulnerability has been used to access the “star account”.
