Anger turned out to be the most universal and functional emotion of a person
Angry expression of the face is biologically versatile for humanity, and every organ involved in its creation is not accidental, but an additional means of expressing the power and thunder, scientists of Australia and the United States found.
About their discoveries, they spoke about their discoveries in Evolution and Human Behavior, and they can briefly be read in a press release from the University of California in Santa Barbary.
Angry expression of the face - shifted and lowered the eyebrows elongated in a thin line pulmonary, blurted nostrils - are equally in all cultures, and even children blind from the birth, who have never seen it, the leading author of the study Aaron Sell points.
As part as part of a major research project dedicated to the nature of wrath, scientists have found that this emotion has arisen to effectively conduct disputes during the conflict.
the more physical damage one person can cause to another, the more opportunities he has to dictate their conditions, and he brings this to the interlocutor with anger.
The researchers have found confirmation of their own other hypothesis: physically strong people are more likely to get angry and switch to contempt, consider themselves entitled to impose unfavourable conditions for others, as well as they prefer forceful methods of resolving conflicts to be peaceful.
Driving up from the fact that anger is primarily an “emotion of bargaining”, the scientists decided that the movements of each of the seven groups of the muscles, creating an anterinary expression of the face, should present an angry individual more powerful and dangerous in the eyes of the interlocutor – and thereby foreclation as soon as possible to agree with its conditions in order to avoid conflict.
To test this hypothesis, the researchers simultured on the computer the faces where each of the seven elements of an angry person was or was absent, and they showed them to informants.
Although lowered eyebrows or advanced chin individually did not make the face angry, then the participants of the study depicted with such traits of a person were recognized as a more physically strong participant of the study unanimously.
The wretch of a person, as in animals, expresses a threat: an exaggerated manifestation of one's own strength, forcing them to agree and obey.
The person inflates the nostrils and tightens the lips for the same purpose as the frog that inflates, or babouin, which demonstrates his fangs.
“The anger “launches” the refusal of the interlocutor to take the situation, and the person immediately takes the form as effectively as possible demonstrating the consequences of this refusal to the opposite side.
But the most astonishing - that none of the components of an angry person is arbitrary, they all express the same thing, ”said anthropologist John Tubey.
The Ministry of communication proposed to allocate 250 million rubles of the television and radio company “Crimea”
The Ministry of communications proposed to allocate 250 million rubles from the federal budget of an autonomous non-commercial uncommercial organization “Tele-Radiocompany “Crimea” in 2014.
This is stated in the draft decree of the government, prepared by the department, which was reviewed by Lenta.ru
In accordance with an explanatory note to the project, subsidies from the federal budget will be aimed "to cover the costs of creating conditions for a large-scale information coverage of the socio-economic situation and the development of a modern information space on the territory of the Republic of the Republic of Crimea, including the acquisition of equipment."
In particular, the allocated money is supposed to re-equate a hardware-study unit, video walls, a central hardware and a video-servatory.
It is also planned to purchase a mobile television station and satellite transmittone.
In addition, from the allocated funds, the company will pay for the use of a fiber-optic communication link (VOLS) and the repair of the energy system.
Subsidies will be provided within the funds of the federal budget provided for the Ministry of Communications.
The state broadcasting company "Crimean" was established in 1959, broadcasts in seven languages: Ukrainian, Russian, Crimean Tatar, German, Greek, Bulgarian and Armenian.
To date, the coverage of a television and radio company with a television and radio company is more than 75 per cent of the territory of the peninsula.
In 2011, "Cream TV and radio company" received a license for television broadcasting in a digital format.
